From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:13:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Read the EC wake cause as one byte

HWAC, the wake cause at EC offset 0x36, is a 16-bit field, as in the OEM
DSDT, but _L1D only tests bits 2, 3, 4 and 7, all in the first byte.
Declare it with 8 bits: one EC read instead of two, and on macOS _L1D no
longer needs a kext that reads wider EC fields (ECEnabler); the battery
methods still do.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/ec.asl | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/ec.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/ec.asl
index be1d7192ff..05990f6bd1 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/ec.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/ec.asl
@@ -7,8 +7,13 @@ Scope (EC)
 {
 	Field (ERAM, ByteAcc, NoLock, Preserve)
 	{
+		/*
+		 * Wake cause. The OEM firmware reads 16 bits, but the bits
+		 * that _L1D tests are all in the first byte: one byte is
+		 * enough, and macOS reads no wider EC field without a kext.
+		 */
 		Offset (0x36),
-		HWAC, 16,	/* Wake cause */
+		HWAC, 8,
 	}
 }
 
